edit('sections/fine_tuning.tex',"Appendix~\\ref{app:G} also justifies GD's empirical small root with vanishing\nmatching error. Substitution of a same-data selected rate for Sign/Adam\nneeds uniform moment convergence, root identification and attainability;\nfixed 24-step bisection alone does not provide them.","Appendix~\\ref{sec:FT-uniform} proves compact-uniform Sign/Adam trajectory,\nloss and training-MSR convergence, so same-data selection is covered.\nA unique population root and vanishing matching residual give root\nconsistency. These root conditions hold analytically for F6's $T=1$\nSign/Adam and $T=4$ Sign; $T=4$ Adam root uniqueness remains conditional.\nFixed 24-step search converges to its population algorithm only under\nstrict decision and cache gaps; it is not exact-root matching.")
edit('main.tex',"In a separate\ncentered cross-entropy first-step regime, $n/d\\to\\gamma>1$, we prove a wrong\ntraining-candidate variance of $1+2c^2/\\gamma$: conditional noise and random\nconditional means contribute equally.","At linear load $n/d\\to\\gamma>1$, we prove the centered cross-entropy\ncoordinate first-step variance $1+2c^2/\\gamma$ and a deterministic\nexact-polar variance limit. A signed envelope yields a unique critical\nstabilizer for the limiting full-training MSR at $\\gamma\\ge16$ and\ncertifies a noise-induced ordering reversal.")
edit('main.tex',"full-training moment and loss-matched MSR comparisons within a residual-only\nclass; a fine-tuning rank law remains open. Experiments distinguish the two\nvariance corrections and preserve finite-dimensional failures. All trajectory\nresults fix time and hyperparameters; finite-load Muon crossings require\nadditional hypotheses.","full-training moments and loss-matched MSR comparisons within a residual-only\nclass. Compact-uniform Sign/Adam convergence permits same-data matching\nunder separated-root conditions; multistep Adam root uniqueness remains\nconditional. A fine-tuning rank law remains open. Experiments retain\nunresolved distributional equivalence and finite-dimensional bias.\nTime is fixed throughout.")
edit('sections/introduction.tex',"This is a full-training moment theorem, without a CE multistep or rank claim.\nFinally, real finite-step updates on a correlated second task admit a moment\nbridge that retains the pretraining--update cross term. Population loss\nmatching yields an MSR comparison within residual-only updates; same-data\nSign/Adam matching and the fine-tuning score distribution require further work.","We also prove the actual exact-polar first-step deterministic variance\nlimit, giving a signed envelope of width $O(\\gamma^{-2})$ and a unique\ncritical stabilizer for the limiting full-training MSR at $\\gamma\\ge16$.\nThis is a moment result; CE multistep and rank laws remain open. Finally,\nreal updates on a correlated second task retain the pretraining--update\ncross term. Compact-uniform Sign/Adam convergence covers same-data\nloss matching under separated-root conditions; multistep Adam root\nuniqueness and the fine-tuning score distribution remain open.")
edit('sections/introduction.tex',"Two-step Sign thresholding and scalar stabilizer roots provide interpretable\nconsequences. The main technical content is the passage from dependent\ntraining trajectories to training scores, and the fixed-load variance\ncorrection. Root certificates and conditional crossing algebra are in the\nappendices.","Our contributions are: (i) real finite-step trajectory reduction and\ntraining-query rank distributions; (ii) both coordinate variance corrections\nand an exact-polar deterministic variance with certified limiting-MSR\nstabilizers; (iii) correlated-task moments and a compact-uniform same-data\nmatching theorem. The appendices provide complete proofs and certificates.")
edit('sections/introduction.tex','Results and their boundaries. All times and hyperparameters are fixed.','Results and their boundaries. Time is fixed; FT also allows selection on fixed compact parameter sets.')
edit('sections/introduction.tex','Full-training margin and variance $1+2c^2/\\gamma$; independent-noise transfer','Coordinate variance $1+2c^2/\\gamma$; exact-polar variance limit; unique limiting-MSR stabilizer for $\\gamma\\ge16$')
edit('sections/introduction.tex','Moments only; fixed dimensionless $e$; Muon finite-load crossings retain F.1/F.2','Moments only; exact polar first step; fixed dimensionless $e$; no finite-sample crossing claim')
edit('sections/introduction.tex',"Weight/loss and both tasks' training MSR; residual-only population-loss comparison","Weight/loss and both tasks' training MSR; compact-uniform Sign/Adam matching")
edit('sections/introduction.tex','No query CLT/rank law; same-data Sign/Adam parameter matching is not covered','No query CLT/rank law; root separation required; multistep Adam root uniqueness conditional')
edit('sections/discussion.tex',"The stabilizer's scalar reference is unconditional, but the finite-load\nMuon envelope is broad and a deterministic crossing additionally requires\nF.2.","The exact-polar deterministic variance and signed envelope now establish\na unique critical stabilizer for the limiting full-training MSR at\n$\\gamma\\ge16$. They give no finite-dataset unique crossing, load\nmonotonicity or rank/recall threshold; practical approximate polar and\nmomentum updates are outside this theorem.")
edit('sections/discussion.tex',"Same-data Sign/Adam matching and a fine-tuning\nCLT/CDF remain open; finite-dimensional rank failures cannot be dismissed\nusing MSR agreement. Frozen experiments support selected mechanisms while\nretaining unresolved intervals and biases. The next distributional problem\nis to carry the two-task moment bridge to query scores and uniformly selected\nparameters, so that practical loss matching can support a retrieval claim.","Compact-uniform convergence permits same-data Sign/Adam selection with\nidentified roots and vanishing matching error. Multistep Adam root\nuniqueness at the experimental target remains conditional, and fixed\n24-step search has only a finite-precision population-algorithm interpretation\nunder strict gaps. FT rank/recall formulas remain conjectures; MSR agreement\ndoes not validate them. W4 supports only 13 of 24 registered CDF equivalence\nclaims, attributes most of the old shared S1 peak to that query subsample,\nand leaves the corrected F6 dimension trend unresolved. The remaining\ndistributional problem is a two-task query CLT/CDF, alongside finite-size\nbias bounds and broader non-Gaussian models.")
edit('sections/experiments.tex',"We report five frozen series, with predictions and rules fixed before each", "We report five original series and the W4 follow-up, with predictions and rules fixed before each")
edit('sections/experiments.tex',"The $d=64$ correct-score variance\nexcess and finite-grid CDF diagnostics remain descriptive (Appendix H).\nA 33-point CDF maximum is only a lower bound on continuous Kolmogorov distance.","W4 directly tests full rank and correct-score CDFs using new seeds and\nmore queries: 13 of 24 registered 4pp equivalence claims are supported,\nwith 11 unresolved. Small empirical CDF errors do not replace corrected\nprecision guarantees. Reconstructing the old S1 data with all queries\nattributes most of its shared variance peak to that particular subsample;\na smaller finite-dimensional excess remains.")
edit('sections/experiments.tex',"A bracket is not a unique\nmoment crossing; the F.1 sufficient envelope is broad at low load.","These empirical brackets differ from the unique limiting-MSR crossing\nproved here. The new interval certificate guarantees strict exterior\nordering and F5's noise endpoint reversal (Appendix~\\ref{app:F}).")
edit('sections/experiments.tex',"Same-data Sign/Adam matching is\nalso outside the fixed-parameter theorem. These results support an MSR\ncomparison while leaving fine-tuning retrieval predictions unproved.","The uniform matching theorem now covers same-data Sign/Adam moments\nunder its root and precision conditions; it does not establish FT retrieval.\nIn W4, fixed-parameter and same-data-matched GD4 have similar negative\nbiases. Their point errors decrease with dimension, but the registered\ncorrected endpoint trend remains unresolved, and a bias is still detected\nat $d=256$. A portable package regenerates F1--F6 representative points\nfrom Gaussian keys/values and rechecks the scalar certificate; it is a\nsmall replay, not a rerun of every original grid.")
